    "1789630872290a78c0": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_d90b719_VKkHG8": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_d90b719",
          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "Dash cam buying guide",
            "title": "What Makes a Good Night Vision Dash Cam?",
            "introduction": "<p>A good night vision dash cam needs more than high resolution. When available light decreases, the camera must capture useful detail while managing image noise, bright headlights, streetlights, shadows, and fast-moving vehicles.</p><p>Several technologies can influence dash cam performance at night.</p><p>Know More at GKU Buying Guides: <a href=\"/blogs/guides/what-makes-a-good-night-vision-dash-cam\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What Makes a Good Night Vision Dash Cam? A Complete Buyer's Guide\">What makes a good night vision dash cam?</a></p><p></p>",
            "sensor_content": "<p>The image sensor plays an important role in low-light recording. Advanced sensors such as Sony <a href=\"/blogs/guides/what-is-sony-starvis-2-everything-you-need-to-know-before-buying-a-dash-cam\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What Is Sony STARVIS 2? Everything You Need to Know Before Buying a Dash Cam\">STARVIS 2</a> are designed to capture more useful image information in challenging lighting conditions, helping produce clearer footage after dark.</p>",
            "hdr_content": "<p>Night driving often combines very bright and very dark areas in the same scene. Headlights, streetlights, signs, and dark roads can create difficult exposure conditions.</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/guides/hdr-vs-wdr-in-dash-cams-whats-the-difference-and-which-is-better\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"HDR vs WDR in Dash Cams: What's the Difference and Which Is Better?\">HDR and WDR</a> help the camera manage these differences so that important areas of the image are less likely to become excessively bright or dark.</p>",
            "resolution_content": "<p>Higher <a href=\"https://www.gkutech.com/blogs/guides/what-dash-cam-resolution-do-you-need-1080p-vs-2k-vs-4k-explained\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.gkutech.com/blogs/guides/what-dash-cam-resolution-do-you-need-1080p-vs-2k-vs-4k-explained\">resolution</a> can preserve more image detail, but resolution alone does not determine night performance. Sensor quality, exposure processing, image signal processing, lens performance, and lighting conditions also matter.</p>",
            "ir_content": "<p>Infrared night vision is particularly useful for interior cameras. IR LEDs can illuminate the vehicle cabin when there is very little visible light, helping the camera record interior activity at night.</p><p>This makes an IR cabin dash cam especially useful for rideshare, taxi, and professional drivers.</p>",
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "section_padding": 64,
            "card_radius": 20,
            "background_color": "#F8F9FD",
